# chunk_node_link_grow.tkr — the COL-F0d `chunk_node_link` fixture (crumb 0024). `main.tks` links
# three fixed chunks (64/128/256 slots) in sequence and reads back each chunk's `CHUNK_NEXT`/
# `CHUNK_CAP`/`CHUNK_USED` header words directly. Exits 0 only if: each chunk's `CHUNK_NEXT` points
# at the PREVIOUS chunk (the first at nothing, `0`) — proving order; each `CHUNK_CAP` matches the
# requested size and `CHUNK_USED` starts at `0` — proving count; and all three addresses are
# distinct — proving each grow allocates a NEW chunk (no whole-backing swap, no value move). The
# compiler holds no `chunk_node_link` callers, so this path is not fixpoint-exercised. Pinned to
# the C backend: `chunk_node_link` emits on the C route only.

Feature: chunk_node_link_grow — chunk_node_link links a new fixed chunk, order and count correct

  Scenario: three_chunks_link_in_order_with_correct_cap_and_used
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
